@* A heading written exactly the way the knowledge panel writes one: the mark
   first, named, with its tooltip off, and the title hard against it with no
   space. The spacing is the stylesheet's.

   It exists because the rule under test is a property of the *pair*, and both
   halves of it at once — the mark has an accessible name, and the heading's
   textContent is what it would have been without the mark. Neither can be
   asserted by rendering the marker on its own. *@

<h4><KnowledgeTypeMarker Value="@Value" CssClass="knowledge-type-marker--leads" Labelled="true" ShowTooltip="false" />@Title</h4>

@code {
    [Parameter]
    public string? Value { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string? Title { get; set; }
}
